+# Cluster ci-1660dea90b5a288f — RowTableViewTest uses the Qt 6-only `itemDelegateForIndex`
+
+**Verdict: REAL (test-side build regression), fixed.** The hosted `linux-x86_64` Qt 5 build stopped at
+`tests/src/gui/RowTableViewTest.cpp:54` and `:57` because `QAbstractItemView::itemDelegateForIndex` does not exist in
+Qt 5. The product class is not involved: `RowTableView` inherits `QTableView`, and these were the only two uses in
+the tree. The test now selects the API by Qt version and keeps the same assertion.
+
+## Evidence
+
+- Hosted CI log `~/.local/share/zene-bunny-fix/qwen/train-ci/31f559ab479dcd1b822545aae477222f58f32c0d/run-43764792400-job-132967358846.log:6694`:
+  `error: 'class lmms::gui::RowTableView' has no member named 'itemDelegateForIndex'; did you mean 'itemDelegateForRow'?`
+  and line 6701 has the second error at `:57`. Lines 6704-6708 are the resulting `gmake` failure of
+  `tests/CMakeFiles/RowTableViewTest.dir`.
+- Qt 5.15 `qabstractitemview.h:226` declares `itemDelegate(const QModelIndex&)`; it has no
+  `itemDelegateForIndex`. Qt 6 `qabstractitemview.h:204-208` deprecates `itemDelegate(index)` in favour of
+  `itemDelegateForIndex(index)`, so an unconditional change to the Qt 5 spelling would break a `-Werror` Qt 6 build.
+- The CI log was produced on the exact pinned commit `31f559ab479dcd1b822545aae477222f58f32c0d`, which is this
+  worktree's `HEAD`. The failure is product-independent: `git grep itemDelegateForIndex` found only the two test
+  uses before the fix.
+
+## Fix
+
+`tests/src/gui/RowTableViewTest.cpp:32-40` adds one local helper:
+
+```cpp
+static const QAbstractItemDelegate* rowDelegate(const RowTableView& view, const QModelIndex& index)
+{
+#if QT_VERSION >= QT_VERSION_CHECK(6, 0, 0)
+	return view.itemDelegateForIndex(index);
+#else
+	return view.itemDelegate(index);
+#endif
+}
+```
+
+Both call sites (`:64`, `:67`) now use it. This is the Qt 5 equivalent of the same query and leaves the assertion
+intact: the delegate on an inserted row is compared with the delegate on the pre-existing row. No product code,
+command, saved data, undo step or audio-thread path is touched.
+
+## Regression proof
+
+The RED is necessarily a compile failure, because the failing translation unit cannot produce a binary. I built the
+exact test translation unit with the system Qt 5.15 (`moc` + `g++ -std=c++20`), the same compiler family the hosted
+Qt 5 job uses. The local configured CMake tree is Qt 6, so it is used for the normal target/ctest proof; the manual
+Qt 5 build is the platform proof for the hosted failure.
+
